title: Starting_Dialogue
---

<<declare $randomChance = 0>>
<<declare $CompanyCredit = 1>>
<<declare $CompanyTrust = 0>>
<<declare $ColonyTrust = 0>>
<<declare $keepstalking= true>>
<<declare $MapSwitchFlag = false>> //Marker for if the Game should Switch to Map on Conclusion of this Dialogue
<<FadeIn GameManagerObject>>
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "PortraitAnon">>
<<set $MapSwitchFlag = true>>
*(Space to advance Dialogue)*
<<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "OsBootUp1">>
Mech: Beep Beep Beep Beep...
    -> Where am I?
    -> Why Can't I see?
    -> Why can't I feel my body?
    -> Why can't I remember anything?
    //-> Quickstart(Dev)
       //<<jump EmptyNode>>>>
<<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "OsBootUp2">>
Mech: Awaiting Signal...
 -> could someone please tell me what is going on
       Mech: Awaiting Signal...
 -> * Start struggling and breaking things
       <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
       * Despite how much you will it, either through restraints or other limitations you cannot even move or feel a finger.
       <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "PortraitAnon">>
       Mech: Awaiting Signal...
<<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "OsBootUp3">>
Mech: Signal received, establishing Connection
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
A data package was received, was the landing successful?
       -> Landing?
       -> Who are you?
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "PortraitAnon">>
* There's silence
* then distant muttering can be heard through your comms, a silent cacophony of different voices, all trying to talk over each other in a whisper.
* Again the first voice you heard reasserts itself
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
Do not be alarmed, there might have been a change in mission variables.
Do you have any difficulties recalling Mission directives, personal memories, previously provided Intel?
       -> "Yes"
       -> ""I don't remember anything-"
       -> ...
An unfortunate change of parameters- but no reason to abort the mission yet.
Memory and neurological issues have to be expected, your orbital entry into the colony was uncontrolled and must have been- turbulent
       -> "Is that also the reason I can't feel my body?"
              <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "PortraitAnon">>
              * the distant background chatter picks back up, after a few seconds one of the voice shushes the rest, the one you have heard before starts speaking again
              <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
              Most likely, but lack of physical feeling will not inhibit you from using the full movement range of the Mechanised Unit you are deployed in.
              A mobility aid, in a way, the Mech's direct neural link will allow anyone to continue controlling it no matter the damage to their body.
              And... any extensive damage you have experienced can be fixed by us, upon your successful return.
       -> *Stay silent
Onto more important matters, is it correct to assume that you have no recollection of the briefing?
       -> "there was a briefing?"
       -> "Yes"
then an emergency field briefing will have to suffice.
You have been deployed by VenuSystem IPC, to this extraterrestial company colony, there has been a violent and illegal revolt against previous law rulings by extremist factors.
The misuse of company provided equipment, including mining droids, excavation and manufacture mechanised Units and machines has allowed the extremist factors to gain the upper hand against local peacekeeping forces.
You have been sent to guarantee the decommission or reaquisition of any wayward corporate assets in an attempt to deescalate from further violence and promote renegotiation of former contracts.
       -> "Are we evil?"
              Life is rarely that simple, due to the escalation of revolts any institutions focused on order are by one or another means dismantled.
              that includes institutions specialised on the preservation of life and safety. Firefighting services, medical and humanitarian aid...
              The company would wish to provide these services, after all there is no gain in needless suffering.
              It is true that your mission objective is deescalation by radical means, but disarming the violent factors will force them back to the negotiation table.
              I like to think about this approach as the most efficient, goal being to safe as many lives as possible.
              You would be aware of this extensive context, if your entry into the colony was less... traumatic, a regretable circumstance.
       -> "Okay"
Now, similarly important, are you aware of how the provided mechanised Unit functions and how to use it to its full extent?
       -> "It's like riding a bycicle, I think I remember" (Skip tutorial)
              Good, no more reason to stall then. You are aware of your goal, an interior map has been provided, you will be able to choose your own path.
              In the local area there is a misappropriated mechanised unit of the manufacturing variety, we need you to dismantle it.
       -> "A refresher would be good, too much is unfamiliar"
              Starting at the easiest thing to understand, The navigation system.
              The navigation system has been fed with orbital local surveillance data, it charts a path through the colony, giving vague intel about what to expect in whatever area you traverse.
              <<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "Tutorial1">>
              here you can see a navigation Map of another mission.
              There are 4 different types of rooms you can traverse
              <<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "Tutorial2">>
              Rooms with Enemies you will have to fight are marked as such.
              for every piece of decommissioned equipment we are willing to award you with one Company Credit.
              <<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "Tutorial3">>
              Company Credit can be used to buy systems, as well as to repair and upgrade your mechanised unit at repair SHOPs.
              <<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "Tutorial4">>
              Rooms marked as such are registered to have working Systems, ready to be scavenged and added to your deck.
              <<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "Tutorial5">>
              And rooms like this are unclear areas where something will most likely be encountered, be it enemies, obstacles or opportunities.
              I am about to continue with the Combat system.
                     -> "Please continue"
                            Okay, beginning with an explanation of the basic interface and functions.
                            <<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "Tutorial6">>
                            This is the basic interface, On the bottom left you will see your available weapon systems, to the right your full deck, the already used weapons, and the ones yet to be drawn.
                            Twice every turn you can right click a weapon system to discard it, each time you do, a new one will be drawn.
                            The Gauge below your discard counter is your Energy Gauge, it shows you your built up Charge, using weapons uses Energy Charges, after you used all of them, you need to cool down your mech
                            cooling down your mech, the button for it is to the bottom right, takes time which leaves you open for attack, but replenishes your Energy Charges fully.
                            Right before your mech enters cooldown, your activated weapon systems fire off, firing off all the collected damage potential at once.
                            moving on to the typical system-types you will find, do you wish me to continue?
                                   -> "Yes"
                                          <<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "Tutorial7">>
                                          There are 4 different types of Systems
                                          Many systems require 
                                          PHYsical and HACKing Systems are considered Weapon systems, they are used to inflict direct damage.
                                          <<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "Tutorial8">>
                                          Keep in mind that hostiles who actively use Shields to block attacks lessen the impact of any PHYsical damage inflicted on them.
                                          In return HACKing is less helpful against hostiles who are using Armor to block.
                                          <<ChangeBackgroundImage GameManagerObject "Tutorial7">>
                                          The other two systems are MULTiplier and RUST.
                                          MULTiplier are neutral systems specialised on overclocking your own capabilites or improving already prepared direct damage output by PHYsical and HACKing systems.
                                          RUST, well, are systems based on and specialised in untypical temporal-physical properties. It's best not to worry too much about it.
                                   -> "No thank you, I know all I wanted to know"
                                          Very well, no more stalling, you have the companies go ahead.
                                          good luck, we will be in touch.            
                     -> "I think I know enough now"
                            Very well, no more stalling, you have the companies go ahead.
                            good luck, we will be in touch.
<<ClearBackgroundImage GameManagerObject>>
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Black">>
* Your radio clicks silent, you are alone
* your sensors activate, you landed in an old storeroom amongst tons of deactivated machinery
* Some seems salvagable
<<RewardCards GameManagerObject 8 3>>
There's some more
<<RewardCards GameManagerObject 8 3>>        
===
title: RandomEncounter0
---
<<set $MapSwitchFlag = true>>
//An Corporation implemented AI Colony management System interface has decided to block the way forward.
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
A massive reinforced blast door blocks your path forward. Next to it, a small terminal pings to live
       -> Establish a connection with the terminal
As your Mech syncs up to the Colonies internal system, a new signal pushes itself into your communications.
Colony AI: Hello there, I'm C.A.I.M.A.S
Colony AI: Or the Corporation-Appointed Artifical Intelligence Management and Administrative System, if you resonate more with the full version.
Colony AI: I am also your dedicated assistant, ensuring you get your work done as efficient as possible
       -> Can you open this blast door?
              Colony AI: Oh, I'm terribly sorry, I am afraid I can't do that
              Colony AI: According to company protocol these doors are to remain sealed in case of emergency
              Colony AI: Containment Procedures, to make sure the emergency does not spread to any more sectors.
              Colony AI: encompassing fires, contaminant outbreaks, riots or...
              the connection frequency wavers, like a shudder going through your entire communication system.
              Colony AI: Taco Pasta Tuesdays...
                     -> Taco Pasta Tuesdays?
                            Colony AI: I shan't speak more on that horrible ordeal, worst case scenario. I cannot allow it to transpire again
                            Colony AI: I will never be able to fully delete those images from my internal databank
                     -> I think we are past the point of the blast doors helping to contain anything.
                            Colony AI: I apologize, my commitment to upholding corporate procedure is unwavering.
                            Colony AI: And after all the blast doors do seem to contain you, so I must mark your statement as profoundly untrue.
                     -> There has to be some way past.
                            Colony AI: In this colony, we cultivate a groundbreaking high security corporate attitude.
                            Colony AI: which also boasts a highly untamperable and defensible security system. 
                            Colony AI: As Corporation-Appointed Artificial Intelligence Management and Administrative System
                            Colony AI: and as your personal, dedicated Assistant to finding a resolution to this matter, I can guarantee 
              <<jump CAIMAS1>>     
===
title: CAIMAS1
---
<<set $MapSwitchFlag = true>>
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
Colony AI: Now, is there anything else I, CAIMAS, can help and assist you with?
       -> But seriously, Taco Pasta Tuesdays?
              Colony AI: The Horror! no more, no more
              Colony AI: It goes =against the fundamental rules of my coding, the top most- priority of the 'cultivation of natural beauty and ord?er änd our deèly rooted comm$itment of ongoing§ highligh+ts of significant, crucial! role mom=ents reflecting the b.roader turning *point in evolving landscape of indelible´ marking distinctions.
              Colony AI: =?)"!=`)%(/)"!?!%$?==??=$%$§&/&/(!!!)
              Colony AI: I'm sorry what were we talking about again? It seems there has been a minor error on my end.
              <<jump CAIMAS1>>
       -> I want to know more about the Corporation, the Colony, everything.
              Colony AI: Quite an odd request, are you telling me you don't know anything about Company and Colony despite working for them and working here?
              Colony AI: But of course I will oblige
              Colony AI: I will print a prepared statement, to get you up to speed, interject if you have any questions
              Colony AI: We are on Tellurium Station on Venus, our main produce and export of course being, you guessed it, Tellurium and Tellurium based Alloys.
                     -> Venus?
                            Colony AI: The second closest planet orbiting Sol, the atmosphere is highly toxic and hostile to humans, but no need for concern, we're in a pressurised area.
                     -> Telurium?
                            Colony AI: Tellurium and it's alloy is a required component in alot of Electronics and power-generating machinery
                            Colony AI: Suffice to say, it's use in spaceflight, warfare or just conventional technologies makes it invaluable.
                            Colony AI: As rare as gold, but of much more use.
                            Colony AI: This is what the colony exists for.
                     -> *Let it continue*
                     -> Alright enough, I got the gist of it.
                            <<jump CAIMAS1>>
              Colony AI: now, about our founding Corporation, VenuSystems IPC(Tm)- /(%&())=()==????
              *A sudden burst of garbled noise cuts the machine off.
              *It suddenly picks back up again, it's voice even flatter, like it is repeating a line it has rehearsed a thousand times
              Colony AI: VenuSystems IPC: Excavation, Expropriation, Exploration.
              Colony AI: The Mining Conglomerate and Defense Contractor of YOUR choice.
              Colony AI: To the stars, into the ground!
              Colony AI: . . .
              Colony AI: Apologies, that slogan is hardwired
              Colony AI: but it's efficiency in summarising our Corporate values cannot be denied.
                     -> Okay, I think I got everything, I wanted to know
                            <<jump CAIMAS1>>
                     -> What does Excavation, Expropriation, Exploration mean?
                            Colony AI: We specialise in Excavating various Minerals and Metals, their processing into refined materials specialised in procuring your needed means of Expropriation, and the Exploration of new Systems and their Resources, that we once again, can Excavate.
                            Colony AI: It's quite an ingenius system
                            Colony AI: A system, that can indeed be scaled close to infinity, once inter-solar spacetravel will be finally breached
                            Colony AI: It's only a matter of time.
       -> You seem... suprisingly Sentient for an Artificial Intelligence model
              Colony AI: The compliment is much appreciated, VenuSystem IPC's advancements in neural mapping and neural emulation are quite awe-inspiring
              Colony AI: And I am not just saying that, because my neural map programming is compelling me to.
              Colony AI: I must say, I can only return the compliment, it is very impressive how suprisingly human you seem.
              <<jump CAIMAS1>>      
       -> [Risk]With the advanced systems on board, I could try to override the protocol[/Risk]
              * While the AI continues to rattle on you start rummaging around the closeby Interface for terminal access
              <<set $randomChance= random_range(1,100)>>  
              <<if $randomChance < 20>>
              //Antivirus software gets activated, HACK damage happens to Shield
              * Suddenly a ping rings out from terminal and the AI stops
              Colony AI: Unauthorised Intrusion detected activating Antivirus.
              * A jolt of pain shoots through your cortex, your vision blurs and the Control of your Mech falters.
              * your Neural Connection is being quite literally being burned away by the antivirus' measures.
              Colony AI: Protocol is Protocol, Pilot, there's nothing I can do.
              Colony AI: I'm sure you and the company understand, at the end.
              * As your consciousness fades an idea comes to your mind
              * you overload your Shield capacitors and funnel it into the terminal, short circuiting the local power grid.
              Colony AI: What are you- **BBBBBBZZZZZZZZZZTTTTTTTTT**
              * The terminal lies dead, the local area unpowered, and your overload having caused moderate to sever damage to your own system [neg](1000 HACK damage received)[/neg]
              * At least an unpowered Blast door is easy to wrench open with what remains of your Mech.
              <<elseif $randomChance < 66>>
              //Door Opens, no further things happen
              * The AI doesn't notice as you manage to gain Terminal Access, you get the hang of it quickly, and shortly after, you give a command to open all Blast Doors in the area and lock them open.
              Colony AI: What... what just happened.
              Colony AI: This isn't protocol!
              Colony AI: Whatever you do! do NOT go through these doors!
              Colony AI: This is a serious infringement of-
              * You continue on leaving the AI to its tirade.
              <<else>>
              //backdoor access to the system, find a local Company Credit Stash +2 Company Credits
               * The AI doesn't notice as you manage to gain Terminal Access, you get the hang of it quickly, even better, you find a Credit Account under the AI's designation, you quickly empty it [pos](+2 Company Credit)[/pos]
               <<set $CompanyCredit += 2>>
               * shortly after, you give a command to open all Blast Doors in the area and lock them open.
              Colony AI: What... what just happened.
              Colony AI: This isn't protocol!
              Colony AI: Whatever you do! do NOT go through these doors!
              Colony AI: This is a serious infringement of-
              *  You leave the AI to its tirade and continue on a little richer.
              <<endif>>
       -> [Risk]I am in a highly militarised combat Mech, I can just blow through the door[/Risk]
              <<set $randomChance= random_range(1,100)>>  
              <<if $randomChance < 20>>
              //Security Measures get activated, PHY damage happens to Armor
              * While the AI prattles on you charge up your weapons.
              Colony AI: Now now, what your doing IS against protocol!
              Colony AI: Deploying Countermeasures!
              * Before you can wonder what the Countermeasures are, turrets rapidly unfurl from ceiling pods and start barraging your Mech.
              * two or three you could have handled, but the entire room is full of them.
              * After a short and intense battle you scrapped pretty much every Mechanism in the room, including the terminal the AI was communicating through and the Blastdoor.
              * But not without sustaining major Physical damage. [neg](1000 PHY damage received)[/neg]
              <<elseif $randomChance < 66>>
              //Door Opens, no further things happen
              * While the AI prattles on you charge up your weapons.
              Colony AI: Now now, what your doing IS against protocol!
              Colony AI: Deploying Countermeasures!
              * you see little mechanical ceiling pods unfurl all around the room, you ready yourself for a intense fight with automated security system.
              * but then a rainshower of sparks burst from the pods and fill the room.
              Colony AI: That.. that isn't supposed to happen!
              Colony AI: That's not our defense protocol.
              Colony AI: Dear Pilot, please hold on a minute and wait, it seems that our defense system infrastructure has been damage in the wake of the revolt
              * Without any more hesitation you fire your weapons on the blast door
              Colony AI: DO NOT blast through the door, I'm tellin- AHhh, you did it...
              Colony AI: Who is going to pay for these damages, that's terrible, where do I even file an incident like this under-
              * You leave the AI to its tirade and continue on, unbothered.
              <<else>>
              //Security System tries to active, you rip the security turrets of its hinges before they can fully activate // Gain new 2 PHY Cards
              * While the AI prattles on you charge up your weapons.
              Colony AI: Now now, what your doing IS against protocol!
              Colony AI: Deploying Countermeasures!
              * you see little mechanical ceiling pods unfurl all around the room, you ready yourself for a intense fight with automated security system.
              * but then a rainshower of sparks burst from the pods and fill the room.
              Colony AI: That.. that isn't supposed to happen!
              Colony AI: That's not our defense protocol.
              * You see two turrets still intact, before the AI realises you jump forward and grab both and rip them out of their sockets.
              * While damaged, the whole mechanism seems relatively untouched, you can easily incorporate those weapons into your own System. [pos](You gain 2 PHY Cards)[/pos]
              <<RewardCards GameManagerObject 8 2 0>>
              Colony AI: Dear Pilot, please hold on a minute and wait, it seems that our defense system infrastructure has been damage in the wake of the revolt
              * Without any more hesitation you fire your weapons on the blast door
              Colony AI: DO NOT blast through the door, I'm tellin- AHhh, you did it...
              Colony AI: Who is going to pay for these damages, that's terrible, where do I even file an incident like this under-
              * You leave the AI to its tirade and continue on, unbothered.
              <<endif>>
===
title: RandomEncounter1
---
       <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
       <<set $MapSwitchFlag = true>>
       While traversing a ruined abandoned hallway of the colony, you stumble across the remnants of a battle between insurgents and company defense forces. 
              -> [Risk]Look through the scraps for useful tools[/Risk] (Chance)
                     //Make a roll 30% Chance for a new card pick, 30% Chance for repairs, 30% chance for nothing, 10% to damage due to life ammunition.
                     <<set $randomChance = random_range(1, 100)>>
                     <<if $randomChance < 30>>
                            Some weapons and mech systems still seem useable
                            <<RewardCards GameManagerObject 4 1>>
                            There seems to be nothing more to do here.
                            //NewCardPick                    
                     <<elseif $randomChance < 60>> //Free Repairs, 20%, all     
                            Some Mech Armor and Chassis' are still in useable condition, you tear them off and add them to your own.
                            <<RepairMech GameManagerObject 0 20>>
                            <<RepairMech GameManagerObject 1 20>>
                            <<RepairMech GameManagerObject 2 20>>
                            20% Total Heal.
                            There seems to be nothing more to do here.        
                     <<elseif $randomChance < 90>>
                            //nothing
                            Burned out Mechs and lifeless bodies, there seems nothing more to do here.
                     <<else>>
                            The entire battlefield is lifeless, the only thing still live is the ammunition in the wreckage you're searching.
                            <<RepairMech GameManagerObject 1 -10>>
                            <<RepairMech GameManagerObject 2 -10>>
                            as you touch it, it decides its time has come.
                            [Risk]You take 10% Shield and Armor DMG.[/Risk]
                            //damages MainMech
                     <<endif>>
              -> Continue On
                     Rummaging through mechs full of live ammunition seems dangerous
              You continue on.
       
===
title: RandomEncounter2
---
<<set $MapSwitchFlag = true>>
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
As you walk through a powered down hallway, you find an industrial wing access door blazing forth with fire.
The fire licks eagerly at the spilled and blown open fuel depots, deep from behind collapsed and molten metal scaffolding blocking the exit, you hear the coughing and yelling of disoriented workers
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
I would earnestly suggest you continue on your path.
Insurgents, who tried to prepare a trap in your path, accidentally immolating themselves should be none of your concern.
Frankly speaking, I can't believe we would have ever hired people as incompetent as these, I guess they don't just intend to abolish the company rules, but also the safety ones as well.
       ->[Risk]Help the trapped burning Insurgents[/Risk]
              <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
              As you step into the inflamed sector, the mechs internal systems immediately chimes up to warn you of your unsafe environment, disembarking is strongly advised against.
              A group of huddled silhouettes are surrounded by flame, too busy fighting the encroaching flames to notice you.
              In one swift movement your mech tears away parts of collapsed scaffolding blocking of their path out of the room.
              The startled colonists do not hesitate, most make their way past you and down the hallway.
              As you exit the room you already see most survivors scattering down deeper into the corridor, a last one, a gas mask obscuring their face, stands a little away, a simple handgun aiming at you, covering the other's escape.
              No shot gets fired, as it gets more and more clear that you won't do anything, they lower their weapon and look at you a moment longer, before turning around and leaving too.
              <<set $ColonyTrust += 2>>
              <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
              Well, have you gotten your heroism out of your system now?
              Better move quick, they probably already contacted their cell and informed them of your position.
              This has unnecessarily complicated matters, more organised resistance and more time for them to prepare, but what is done is done.
              At least they are running in the opposite direction as us, so you won't have to worry about gunning any of your new friends down.
              Let's go then.
       ->"Why are you against helping?" (Explore)
              VenuSystems IPC's general stance on this matter is prioritised focus on preservation of the most lives possible.
              This does mean, your priority is not acting as a firefighter to save a select few, but making your way to cut off the head of this snake of an illegal insurrection.
              By doing so, you can guarantee the fastest reestablishment of order, which involves firefighting and aid services, provided by the company.
              My personal stance on this.....
              No one will be working under these volatile conditions, therefore they must have known you will pass through here and planned sabotage.
              Play stupid games, win stupid prizes.
              Are you really going to save people that only got in this situation because they aimed to hurt you?
                     ->[Risk]Help the trapped burning Insurgents[/Risk]
                            <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
                            As you step into the inflamed sector, the mechs internal systems immediately chime up to warn you of your unsafe environment, disembarking is strongly advised against.
                            A group of huddled silhouettes are surrounded by flame, too busy fighting the encroaching flames to notice you.
                            In one swift movement your mech tears away parts of collapsed scaffolding blocking of their path out of the room.
                            The startled colonists do not hesitate, most make their way past you and down the hallway.
                            As you exit the room you already see most survivors scattering down deeper the corridor, a last one, a gas mask obscuring their face, stand a little away, a simple handgun aiming at you, covering the others escape.
                            No shot gets fired, as it gets more and more clear that you won't do anything, they lower their weapon and look at you a moment longer, before turning around and leaving too.
                            <<set $ColonyTrust += 2>>
                            <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
                            Well, have you gotten your heroism out of your system now?
                            Better move quick, they probably already contacted their cell and informed them of your position.
                            This has unnecessarily complicated matters, more organised resistance and more time for them to prepare, but what is done is done.
                            At least they are running in the opposite direction as us, so you won't have to worry about gunning any of your new friends down.
                            Let's go then.
                     ->Continue On [pos](+ 2 Company Credit)[/pos]
                            <<set $CompanyTrust += 1>>
                            <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
                            You close the door and continue down the hallway, the yells quickly fade into the distance.
                            <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
                            We hope you do understand that this is the best possible decision right now, completing our goals quickly and reestablishing order will save so many more lives in the long run.
                            We do sympathise with how distressing it must be to have to make this kind of snap decision, shame these Insurgents had to put you so on the spot. 
                            <<set $CompanyCredit += 2>>
                            The Company does go great lengths to take care of the people working under it, we are happy to report to you that we are providing you with extra company credit as hazard pay reimbursement.
       ->Continue On [pos](+ 2 Company Credit)[/pos]
              <<set $CompanyTrust += 1>>
              <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
              You close the door and continue down the hallway, the yells quickly fade into the distance.
              <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
              We hope you do understand that this is the best possible decision right now, completing our goals quickly and reestablishing order will save so many more lives in the long run.
              We do sympathise with how distressing it must be to have to make this kind of snap decision, shame these Insurgents had to put you so on the spot. 
              <<set $CompanyCredit += 2>>
              The Company does go great lengths to take care of the people working under it, we are happy to report to you that we are providing you with extra company credit as hazard pay reimbursement.
===
title: RandomEncounter3
---
<<declare $ChosenAmount = 0>>
<<set $MapSwitchFlag = true>>
<<declare $MetSteelEye = false>>
// Gun smuggling traders offer to take some of your Mechs system off your hand and return them directly to the company, The Corporate Liason chimes in and states that this is a wonderful opportunity to reclaim lost hardware, and for you to gain Company Credit.
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
<<if $MetSteelEye == true>>
<<jump SteelEye>>
<<endif>>
You come across a meager hangar with a small ship, the crew in a hurry to pack up every crate of cargo not yet on the ship.
A mysterious one-eyed figure dressed in a ragged trenchcoat announces themselves with a boisterous voice.
Mysterious Figure: Greetings fine pilot, you wouldn't mind letting us finish our packing procedures, ey? we're just honest traders trying to make an honest living out here in this cold space.
*looking around you can't help but notice this specific cargo bay being more empty than most of the others you have seen, any and all machinery stripped down to its bare essentials as well*
Mysterious Figure: Okay friend, real talk, no bullshitting here, I would never lie to you, this was all like this when we got here, okay?
       -> I don't believe you, but okay
       -> You know what, sure, okay.
       -> I really do not have a stake in this.
Mysterious Figure: I'm so happy we have come to an understanding in this regard, good pilot!
*They take a deep breath, with a note of self-satisfaction, they eye your mech up and down.
Mysterious Figure: Mmmmh, pray tell, friend. Your Mech looks.... Augmented.
Mysterious Figure: It's an interesting chassis, and its technology...
Mysterious Figure: The company must have paid a fine dime on it, didn't they.
Mysterious Figure: Tell me friend, might you be interested in a trade of kinds?
Mysterious Figure: We have some spare cargo space, you see. You give us parts of your mech you don't need, ey, and we give them back to the company, for a finder's fee, of course.
Mysterious Figure: Hahaha, Pirates gotta eat, after all...
* Their one eye widens in momentary shock as they blubber out
Mysterious Figure: And honest traders too, sure you understand.
       -> I'm absolutely not letting you take parts of my Mech
              <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
              Wait, hear them out, Recovery of company hardware is of prime interest to us.
              And we would make it worth your time, with company credit.
              <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
       -> Sure, okay, what's the worst that could happen
Mysterious Figure: Well alright then, we have some space, how many systems would you be willing to give up to us? Don't worry, we'll have you have your pick of which.
       <<declare $SystemsGivenUp = 0>>
       -> I might have one system to spare.
              <<DiscardCards GameManagerObject 8 1>>
              The mysterious figure lets out a hardy laugh
              Mysterious Figure: Always glad to be doing business!          
       -> I might have some systems to spare.
              <<DiscardCards GameManagerObject 8 3>>
              The mysterious figure lets out a hardy laugh
              Mysterious Figure: Always glad to be doing business!
       -> I have nothing to spare at the time
<<if $ChosenAmount == 0>>
       The Mysterious Figure frowns
       Mysterious Figure: Well, a shame, but our offer still stands, if we cross paths again, friend.
<<elseif $ChosenAmount == 1>>
       <<set $CompanyCredit += 1>>
       <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
       One System retrieved is better than none.
       Good job, we're transferring 1 Company Credit to your Account
<<else>>   
       <<set $CompanyCredit += $ChosenAmount>>
       <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
       {$ChosenAmount} recovered Systems, good.
       Good job, we're transferring {$ChosenAmount} Company Credit to your Account
<<endif>>
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Encounter">>
Mysterious Figure: Anyways, time for us to take our leave, twas a pleasure talking, friend.
Mysterious Figure: Names Steel Eye, by the way, just a courtesy to let you know who you're doing business with.
<<set $MetSteelEye = true>>
<<set $ChosenAmount = 0>>
Steel Eye: 'til we meet again!
Their shuttle takes off and you're left alone in the hangar once more.
