===
title: BossConversation
---
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "BlueCollar">>
Good, you actually stopped fighting
I didn't actually expect that
the last few didn't listen
       -> "What do you mean last few?"
              Oh come on, don't expect you're the first they sent here.
              They keep sending more, you probably won't be the last either
       -> "then talk."
              You're not the first and won't be the last-
       -> "I am making a mistake."
              Well, at least you are listening
              You are not the first nor last they used
And they didn't actually send you here
       -> "what?"
not in the physical sense...
I cracked open plenty that came before, like I said.
and you know there's no company present here, they got chased off a while ago, we've just been cleaning after the mess they've left.
They don't have the resources to return, or it's just not profitable enough for them to.
Instead they opted for the cheaper alternative, you!
Every few days, one of the stored mechs receives a signal, goes haywire and goes on a destruction spree.
       -> That means...
You're a neural scan, sorry
No body for you to get fixed
sending out a data transfer is cheaper and faster than sending their own forces.
Good news is, they have no sway here, over you
       -> this is alot to take in
It is...
<<FadeIn GameManagerObject>>
tell me, have they chimed up in your comms by now, called me a liar or anything like that.
If not, they probably pulled the plug and are already preparing the next copy to send over.
       -> I don't quite know what to do now
       -> "Do I get anything for the Company Credit I collected."
              Nah, that stuff is totally worthless.
                     -> "Dangit"
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Black">>
Lacking a body sucks, I'm sorry, you got the next best thing though.
And lucky for you we are in need of any capable hands that can pilot.
You can make the chaos you caused up to us.
===
title: CorporateEnding
---
<<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "TheCorporation">>
<<FadeIn GameManagerObject>>
Fabulous work, we knew you were right for the job!
       -> "It's over, does that mean you'll fix my body"
              you more than exceeded our expectation, upper management was skeptical about your potential and performance.
              And now look at you, completed the main objective, gathered equipment and systems, you did an excellent job.
              you will get something even better than a fixed, limited biological body
              the scalability of it all...
              A model like you could be deployed all over contested territories, unleashed to spread controlled chaos.
              You are a fine specimen.
                     -> "I feel weak-"
                            <<PilotSprite GameManagerObject "Black">>
                            Don't worry, recovery is already underway.
                            There's still much to be done, alot of Bureaucracy too, you will get your reward.
                            For now, we recommend you let your Unit enter sleep mode.
                            Disconnected from the power grid, it must be almost out of battery
                            

